[0.171, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mDeclined\u001b[12Gto\u001b[15Ganswer\u001b[22GClaude's\u001b[31Gquestions:\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  · Who makes a venue's `production` rows (Ore's furs, Forge's grain), and who owns the output? (Regional employer \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m(Rec\u001b[11Gm\u001b[13Gended)\u001b[20G/ Th\u001b[25G broker produces)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m· No wage amounts or batch\u001b[33Glengths are authored, and raw production has no recipe. How should W04 handle payroll? \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B(Daily batches, wage\u001b[27Gshare\u001b[33G/ Split: payroll later)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m· How does a region's \u001b[29Gousehold pool buy its essentials (and optional goods, the venue's `demand` rows) when goods \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Btrade\u001b[12Gin whole totes but each interval's\u001b[47Gneed i\u001b[54G fraction\u001b[64Gl?\u001b[67G(Thr\u001b[72Gugh\u001b[76Gthe book (Recommende\u001b[97G) / Direct, fractional)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m· Th\u001b[12Geight-good \u001b[24Grading\u001b[31Gfixture t\u001b[41Gades no gra\u001b[53Gn, w\u001b[58Gter or medical supplies, so its two r\u001b[96Ggions could never meet a \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bneed.\u001b[12GWhat sh\u001b[20Guld h\u001b[26Gppen\u001b[31Gthere? (Nee\u001b[43G not requ\u001b[53Gred / Add ess\u001b[67Gnti\u001b[72Gs / Let them starve)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mYour\u001b[8Gfirst\u001b[14Gthree\u001b[20Ganswers\u001b[28Gare\u001b[32Gnoted:\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G- \u001b[1mProducer:\u001b[22m a r\u001b[19Ggional employer per\u001b[39Gregion,\u001b[47Gselling\u001b[55Gto\u001b[58Gthe\u001b[62Gbroker\u001b[69Gthrough\u001b[77Gthe\u001b[81Gbook.\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mWages:\u001b[22m daily batches, each with a\u001b[39Gwa\u001b[42Ge bill that is an auth\u001b[65Gr\u001b[67Gd\u001b[69Gs\u001b[71Gare of the \u001b[83Gutput's\u001b[91Gvalue.\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mHouseholds:\u001b[22m they buy whole\u001b[32Gto\u001b[35Ges through the book and consume the exact amount from a\u001b[91Gp\u001b[93Gntry.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BWhat\u001b[8Gwould\u001b[14Gyou\u001b[18Glike\u001b[23Gto\u001b[26Gclarify\u001b[34Gabout\u001b[40Gthe\u001b[44Gtrading\u001b[52Gfixture?\u001b[61GIts\u001b[65Gtwo\u001b[69Gregions\u001b[77G(Ore\u001b[82GHighlands\u001b[92Gand\u001b[96GBrine\u001b[102GCoast,\u001b[109G25,000\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bpeople each) trade only metals, furs, sal\u001b[45G, l\u001b[49Gme, glassware and soap. Without grain, water or medical \u001b[106Gupplies they\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bcan n\u001b[9Gv\u001b[11Gr mee\u001b[17G \u001b[19G need.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m✻\u001b[3GCogitated for 1m 59s · done 3:53 pm\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;136;136;136m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m❯ They need to also trade the essentials. I just wanted to confirm that this is for manifest and not the cut-down game\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
